course: dictionary
lesson: 14644
title: Coming just before
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Preceding means coming just before something in time, order or position. When you meet it, ask yourself: what came first? «The preceding page had a map of the island.» The page before the one you are reading is the preceding page.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «In the preceding question, you added two numbers.» The question before the one you are now answering is the preceding question. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the question just before" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Preceding also works in maths and stories. In maths, the number preceding 50 is 49, because 49 comes just before 50 when you count. In a story, «The storm was preceded by hours of heavy rain» tells you the rain came first, before the storm.
fact: Preceding means coming just before something.
fact: «The preceding day» means the day before.
fact: The number preceding 50 is 49.
fact: «In the preceding weeks» means in the weeks just before now.
fact: Precede is the verb, meaning to come before; preceding is its form and can also work as an adjective.
exercise: «The preceding page had a map of the island.» What does preceding mean here? | Coming just after | *Coming just before | Written in red ink | Torn out of the book
exercise: What number is preceding 50? | 5 | 51 | 500 | *49
exercise: «In the preceding question, you added two numbers.» Which question does this mean? | The next question | A question about animals | *The question just before | The last question of the test
test: «The storm was preceded by hours of heavy rain.» Which came first? | *The rain | Both at once | The storm | Neither
test: «We finished the preceding chapter before lunch.» Which chapter did we finish? | *The chapter just before this one | The first chapter of the book | The chapter after this one | The last chapter of the book
exam: In «the preceding weeks», what does preceding mean? | *Just before now | Far in the future | Lost forever | Happening at the same time
